Description: ISO builder and customizer for Debian-based distributions
 Eduka-Customizer builds live images of your own Debian-based distribution
 from Debian stable, testing, sid or a Debian derivative such as LMDE. It
 extracts a Debian live ISO (or bootstraps a new Debian base, or snapshots
 the running system) and guides you step by step: repositories, identity,
 users, language, desktop or window manager in a Mini, Compact, Full or
 Full-with-apps edition (GNOME, KDE Plasma, Xfce, Cinnamon, MATE, LXQt,
 LXDE, Budgie, Enlightenment, Eduka-Desktop, i3, Sway, labwc and more),
 packages and Flatpak applications, replacing the default applications,
 kernel, boot menu, themes, the Plymouth boot splash, login screen,
 wallpaper and the Calamares installer. Checks before building stop what
 would break the ISO. It can edit the system live in a nested window and
 builds a hybrid BIOS/UEFI ISO that can be tested in QEMU.
 .
 Earlier versions made only Edukasaun OS; the Edukasaun OS defaults are
 gone and every name is yours to choose.
 .
 It also builds your own branding packages (replacing the identity of
 base-files, lsb-release, distro-info-data, desktop-base, the Debian logos,
 GRUB and the Calamares installer) and lets you edit any installed Debian
 package directly in the Package Workshop.
 .
 Eduka-Customizer runs on Debian, Debian derivatives, Ubuntu and
 Ubuntu-based systems. The images it builds are always Debian-based
 (Debian stable, testing, sid and derivatives); Ubuntu-based images are not
 supported as a source.
